  ============================================================ -->
<section id="faq" class="section">
  <div class="section-inner max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold text-center mb-8" data-i18n="section.faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <%
        var faqs = [
          { q:'Do I need an app to scan a SafeTag?',
            a:'No app, ever — for either the owner or the rescuer. Any modern phone camera opens the emergency profile by scanning the QR code. Phones with NFC can also tap the built-in RFID chip. The rescuer just points their camera or brings their phone close. That\'s it.' },
          { q:'What if the QR code gets scratched or damaged?',
            a:'This is the question we get most. Every SafeTag has a built-in RFID/NFC chip — completely independent of the printed QR. If the QR is scratched, wet, faded, or the tag is used in darkness, a rescuer can tap their NFC-enabled phone to the chip and instantly open the same emergency profile. One physical tag. Two ways to save a life.' },
          { q:'How does the RFID/NFC chip work?',
            a:'The NFC chip inside every SafeTag is pre-programmed with a secure URL pointing to the owner\'s emergency profile. When an NFC-enabled smartphone (most Android and iPhone 7+ models) is held near the tag, the phone reads the chip and opens a browser tab automatically — no scanning required. It works in darkness, at any angle, and in wet conditions.' },
          { q:'Can I update the information after buying?',
            a:'Yes. Sign in to your dashboard and update the profile at any time. Changes go live in seconds on both the QR link and the NFC chip URL — no need to replace or reprogram the physical tag.' },
          { q:'Is my personal information private?',
            a:'Your emergency profile is only accessible when someone physically scans your tag or taps the NFC chip — it cannot be found by searching the internet. We never share your data with third parties. Only people who have your physical tag in their hand can access your profile.' },
          { q:'Can I use it for my pet?',
            a:'Yes. Select "PET" as the category and enter your own contact details as the emergency contact. Any finder can scan the QR or tap the NFC chip to reach you immediately — no separate pet-finding app needed.' },
          { q:'Do you do bulk orders for schools or hospitals?',
            a:'Yes. Batches of up to 10,000 tags can be created at once with a CSV export containing QR codes, NFC payloads, and unique tag IDs. Contact us via the manufacturer portal. Hospitals and first-responder teams particularly benefit from the NFC chip — scannable even when a patient is unconscious.' },
        ];
        faqs.forEach(function(f){ %>
        <details class="card p-5 cursor-pointer group">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-navy text-lg list-none flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
            <%= f.q %>
            <span class="text-brand text-xl flex-shrink-0 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600"><%= f.a %></p>
        </details>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

